Z||000000||kempo||08-25-2001||09:18 PM||||The check engine light will come on at low rpms, say I am cruising in a residential area for 5 minutes, speed limit of 25, in say fourth gear...  after about 35-40 seconds of this, the check engine light will come on, and stay on until I get back on the rpms and wind it out a bit.  It will also come on for long idle periods.  My gas mileage has dropped considerably.  I used to get 250-300 miles highway driving easy on a tank of gas.  To which has now dropped to a horrible 150-165 miles on a tank of gas.  This is real crappy!  I have a 3.4L camaro v6 engine lined up to put in the fiero sometime in November, but I don't know if it's the engine that is causing bad gas mileage?  Tires have correct pressure, yadda yadda yadda...  <P>1- Why is my check engine light coming on?<BR>2- Could the engine be the reason for bad mpg?<P>-Kemp<BR>87 Fiero GT / 5 spd<BR>133k miles||||reg||1
