Z||000002||kempo||08-27-2001||03:51 PM||||Probably a stupid question from an uninformed fiero owner (aka- me), how do I check the codes?||||reg||1
Z||000003||Ken Wittlief||08-27-2001||04:02 PM||||you get a torx 15 bit, and take off the plastic cover the cig lighter is in. Take a paper clip and bend it into a U shape and, with the key off, put it in the lower two holes on the passenger side of the connector you see in there.<P>  turn your key to run (not start) and watch the check engine light - it will blink out 2 digit number codes, each code is repeated 3 times [ie blink blink........blink  is 21]<BR>then goto this site and it will tell you what the codes mean:<P>oops! i deleted the link from my folder - goto yahoo and search for Fiero Online service manual - its easy to find - the codes are in there.<P>or come back here and someone will tell you what the code means.<P> I'll bet you have a vacuum leak somewhere and its screwing up a sensor.||||reg||1
Z||000004||ray b||08-27-2001||04:03 PM||||in the console between the seats under a cover is the diagnostic link, short the A and B terminals [paper clip works] and the ck eng lite will flash [blink] the codes<BR>use the search on this forum to get the code list and better how to.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
